   "html_text": "We have seen that Dietrich viewed the complexity of the universe of being as itself a likeness to God. The world in all of its wonderful complexity revealed something of God to a mind willing to inquire into it, giving glory to God in its very complexity. Perhaps Dietrich’s metaphysical vision of the universe explains his keen interest in science, an interest that led him to write treatises summing up his research into light and color and into the material elements of the universe. At any rate, ",
